WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.804
Welcome to Module 1 of the
Provider Notices learning path:

2
00:00:03.804 --> 00:00:05.837
why provider notices go unread.

3
00:00:05.837 --> 00:00:11.316
Every cloud provider tells the agency, in
writing and ahead of time, what it will

4
00:00:11.316 --> 00:00:16.625
change, retire or patch in the agency's
own tenant, account, tenancy or project.

5
00:00:16.625 --> 00:00:21.475
The notices land in a portal or one
person's inbox, and nobody owns them.

6
00:00:21.475 --> 00:00:26.103
This path teaches you to read each
provider's notices from its own record,

7
00:00:26.103 --> 00:00:29.574
hold every notice as one
record, give the ones that need

8
00:00:29.574 --> 00:00:32.813
action an owner and a due
date, and keep the evidence.

9
00:00:32.813 --> 00:00:37.020
It follows the seven gates of the
provider notices implementation guide,

10
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.262
with the developer workbook
Building Provider Notices.

11
00:00:40.262 --> 00:00:42.713
This first module comes before the gates.

12
00:00:42.713 --> 00:00:46.387
It takes about forty-five
minutes, with a lab on fixtures.

13
00:00:46.387 --> 00:00:51.940
The code is illustrative: tested against
fixtures, not run against a live tenant.
